HUMAN RESOURCES POLICY & PROCEDURES MANUAL

Yanbu Aramco Sinopec Refining Company (YASREF)

Document No.: HR-POL-001 | Version: 1.0

IMPORTANT NOTICE: This is an illustrative policy document prepared for reference and academic or professional purposes. It is not an official YASREF policy, does not reproduce confidential company documents, and must not be represented as an approved company publication.

1. PURPOSE

The purpose of this Human Resources Policy Manual is to establish a consistent framework for managing employees, developing human capital, promoting employee welfare, and ensuring compliance with applicable laws and organizational requirements.

The policy aims to:

Attract, recruit, and retain qualified employees.
Promote fairness, transparency, and equal employment opportunities.
Establish consistent HR practices and procedures.
Enhance employee performance and organizational productivity.
Support employee learning, development, and career progression.
Maintain a safe, respectful, and productive working environment.
Align human capital strategies with the company's business objectives.
2. SCOPE

This policy applies to all eligible employees of the Company, including permanent and fixed-term employees, subject to their employment contracts and applicable company regulations.

Certain provisions may differ for contractors, consultants, temporary personnel, and other third-party workers.

3. HUMAN RESOURCES GUIDING PRINCIPLES

The Human Resources Department shall conduct its activities in accordance with the following principles:

3.1 Safety: Promote a safe working environment and ensure that employees comply with occupational health, safety, security, and environmental requirements.

3.2 Commitment: Encourage employees to demonstrate dedication toward organizational objectives and responsibilities.

3.3 Integrity: Maintain honesty, transparency, confidentiality, and ethical conduct in all employment-related matters.

3.4 Collaboration: Promote teamwork, mutual respect, and effective communication across departments.

3.5 Excellence: Encourage continuous improvement, professional development, and high performance.

4. RECRUITMENT AND SELECTION POLICY

4.1 General Policy

The Company shall recruit qualified candidates based on organizational requirements, approved manpower plans, job specifications, and competency requirements.

Recruitment decisions shall be based on merit, qualifications, experience, professional competencies, and suitability for the position.

4.2 Recruitment Procedures

The requesting department identifies a manpower requirement.
The department submits an approved manpower requisition to Human Resources.
Human Resources reviews the position requirements and budget availability.
Vacancies are advertised through approved recruitment channels.
Candidates undergo screening, interviews, and assessments as appropriate.
The selected candidate undergoes the required employment checks and approvals.
An employment offer is issued to the successful candidate.
The employee completes the onboarding and joining formalities.
4.3 Equal Employment Opportunity

The Company shall promote fair employment practices and prohibit unlawful discrimination in recruitment, selection, promotion, and other employment decisions.

5. EMPLOYMENT AND ONBOARDING POLICY

5.1 Employment Documentation

New employees shall provide the required employment documentation, including identification, educational qualifications, professional certifications, and other documents required by the Company and applicable regulations.

5.2 Employee Orientation

All newly hired employees shall participate in an onboarding program covering:

Company vision, mission, and organizational values.
Organizational structure and departmental responsibilities.
HR policies and employment procedures.
Occupational health, safety, and environmental requirements.
Information security and confidentiality.
Employee rights, responsibilities, and benefits.
5.3 Probationary Period

The probationary period shall be specified in the employment contract and administered in accordance with applicable Saudi Labor Law.

6. WORKING HOURS AND ATTENDANCE POLICY

6.1 Working Hours

Working hours shall be established according to the employee's employment category, approved work schedule, operational requirements, and applicable Saudi Labor Law.

Employees assigned to refinery operations, shift work, or emergency-response duties shall follow their approved operational schedules.

6.2 Attendance

Employees are expected to:

Report to work according to their assigned schedules.
Record attendance using the approved attendance system.
Obtain approval for planned absences.
Notify their supervisor of unexpected absence or lateness.
Comply with overtime and shift-rotation procedures.
6.3 Overtime

Overtime must be authorized by the appropriate management authority and compensated in accordance with company regulations and applicable labor legislation.

7. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS POLICY

7.1 General Policy

The Company shall maintain a structured compensation and benefits framework designed to attract, motivate, and retain qualified employees while supporting internal equity and market competitiveness.

7.2 Salary Administration

Employee salaries shall be determined based on relevant factors, including:

Job grade and position responsibilities.
Employee qualifications and experience.
Relevant market benchmarks.
Internal salary structures.
Approved compensation budgets.
7.3 Employee Benefits

Subject to eligibility and approved company programs, employee benefits may include:

Medical insurance coverage.
Housing-related benefits or programs.
Transportation-related allowances.
Job-related allowances.
Ramadan allowance, where applicable.
Thrift or savings programs.
Annual leave and other statutory leave entitlements.
End-of-service benefits.
Professional training and development opportunities.
All benefits shall be administered according to the applicable employment contract, approved benefit plans, and company regulations.

7.4 Payroll Administration

The Human Resources and Finance Departments shall coordinate to ensure that employee salaries, approved allowances, deductions, and other payments are processed accurately and on time.

8. LEAVE AND HOLIDAY POLICY

8.1 Annual Leave

Employees shall be entitled to annual leave in accordance with their employment contracts, approved company regulations, and applicable Saudi Labor Law.

Employees must submit leave requests through the approved HR system and obtain the required approval before commencing leave, except in emergency circumstances.

8.2 Sick Leave

Employees may be granted sick leave upon submission of appropriate medical documentation and in accordance with applicable regulations.

8.3 Official Holidays

Employees shall receive official holidays in accordance with the applicable laws and approved company calendar.

8.4 Other Leave

Other categories of leave may include:

Maternity leave.
Paternity leave.
Marriage leave.
Bereavement leave.
Examination leave.
Unpaid leave.
Other legally recognized leave entitlements.
9. PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT POLICY

9.1 Objective

The performance management system aims to evaluate employee contributions, identify development opportunities, and align individual performance with organizational objectives.

9.2 Performance Evaluation

Employee performance shall be assessed using established performance objectives, key performance indicators, and competency requirements.

Performance evaluations may consider:

Achievement of agreed objectives.
Quality and efficiency of work.
Compliance with safety requirements.
Technical and professional competencies.
Teamwork and collaboration.
Leadership and behavioral competencies.
9.3 Performance Review Process

Establish annual performance objectives.
Communicate performance expectations.
Conduct periodic performance reviews.
Evaluate results against established KPIs.
Provide feedback and development recommendations.
Establish improvement plans where necessary.
Document and approve final performance assessments.
10. TRAINING AND DEVELOPMENT POLICY

10.1 General Policy

The Company recognizes employee development as an important component of sustainable organizational performance.

Training activities shall support operational requirements, employee competencies, professional development, and future workforce needs.

10.2 Training Programs

Training opportunities may include:

Technical and operational training.
Health, Safety, Security, and Environmental (HSSE) training.
Leadership and management development.
Professional certification programs.
Digital and information technology training.
Communication and interpersonal skills.
Succession planning and talent development.
10.3 Training Evaluation

Training effectiveness shall be evaluated through appropriate assessment methods, employee feedback, competency improvement, and performance outcomes.

11. PROMOTION AND CAREER DEVELOPMENT POLICY

Employee promotion and career progression shall be based on objective criteria, organizational requirements, employee performance, qualifications, competencies, experience, and availability of approved positions.

The Company may implement:

Career development plans.
Job evaluation and grading.
Succession planning.
Internal mobility.
Leadership development programs.
Talent identification and retention initiatives.
All promotions shall follow the applicable approval and authorization process.

12. EMPLOYEE RELATIONS AND DISCIPLINARY POLICY

12.1 Employee Conduct

Employees are expected to maintain professional behavior and demonstrate integrity, respect, accountability, and commitment to organizational values.

12.2 Prohibited Conduct

Examples of misconduct include:

Violation of company policies and procedures.
Unauthorized disclosure of confidential information.
Workplace harassment or discrimination.
Fraud, dishonesty, or conflicts of interest.
Unauthorized absence.
Violation of safety requirements.
Misuse of company property or resources.
12.3 Disciplinary Procedures

Disciplinary actions shall be administered fairly and consistently, following an appropriate investigation and employee response process.

Any disciplinary measure must comply with applicable Saudi Labor Law and approved company regulations.

13. HEALTH, SAFETY, SECURITY, AND ENVIRONMENT POLICY

Due to the nature of refinery operations, the Company shall maintain a strong safety culture and require employees to comply with all applicable HSSE requirements.

Employees shall:

Follow approved safety procedures.
Wear the required personal protective equipment.
Participate in mandatory safety training.
Report unsafe conditions and incidents.
Follow emergency response instructions.
Comply with environmental protection requirements.
Participate in relevant safety awareness programs.
No operational or production objective shall justify knowingly disregarding critical safety requirements.

14. EMPLOYEE GRIEVANCE POLICY

The Company shall provide employees with appropriate channels to raise workplace concerns and complaints.

Employees may submit grievances concerning:

Employment conditions.
Workplace relationships.
Performance evaluation.
Compensation and benefits.
Disciplinary decisions.
Workplace discrimination or harassment.
Other employment-related matters.
Human Resources shall review submitted grievances objectively, maintain confidentiality as appropriate, and coordinate with relevant departments to facilitate resolution.

15. EMPLOYEE DATA AND CONFIDENTIALITY POLICY

Employee information shall be collected, processed, maintained, and disclosed only for legitimate business, employment, or legal purposes.

Access to employee records shall be restricted to authorized personnel.

Employees and HR representatives shall maintain the confidentiality of sensitive company and employee information in accordance with applicable policies and regulations.

16. SEPARATION FROM EMPLOYMENT POLICY

Employment separation may occur through:

Voluntary resignation.
Retirement.
Expiration of an employment contract.
Mutual agreement.
Termination in accordance with applicable law.
Other legally recognized circumstances.
Human Resources shall coordinate the separation process, including:

Verification of the separation request or decision.
Confirmation of the employee's final working date.
Completion of the handover process.
Return of company property and access credentials.
Settlement of outstanding financial obligations.
Calculation and payment of applicable final entitlements.
Completion of exit formalities and documentation.
17. POLICY COMPLIANCE AND REVIEW

All employees and relevant management personnel are responsible for complying with the applicable provisions of this manual.

The Human Resources Department shall periodically review the policies to ensure their continued relevance, effectiveness, and alignment with:

Company business strategies.
Applicable Saudi Labor Law.
Relevant government regulations.
Organizational requirements.
Industry best practices.
Any amendments shall be reviewed and approved by the appropriate company authority before implementation.

18. APPROVAL AND AUTHORIZATION

This illustrative policy manual is subject to formal review and approval before adoption.


